Actually, this is not true.
There is no physical diiference between the 2 versions, other than the
firmware BIOS, and whether or not it is packaged with a Digital license and
copy of DEC UNIX. The Unix, however, is not cheap.
Physically they are the CPU's and boards other than the ROM code.

The part # for a PCI164 300MHz Alpha motherboard and CPU with 2MB L2 cache is
 EBP41-AN for ARC console (NT &  Linux)version, NO Operating system.
 EBP41-AZ for UNIX version, c/w DEC UNIX and 2 user license.

Costs (From a DEC TOEM, such as ourselves) are :
 EBP41-AN :     $ 5,890      (U.S.Dollars)
 EBP41-AZ :     $ 12,869     (U.S.Dollars)

Delivery is a bit long, currently, at 2 to 4 weeeks.

