Here's an excerpt from an email between myself and Vincent Ledoux (chief
support engineer, Digital of Canada) on the new boards coming from Digital.
Please note that we are being told that once again, the boards are the same,
other than the PROMs and UNIX license choice.

Vincent Ledoux of Digital Equipment of Canada (email address is private)wrote:
"We just announced the 500 Mhz 21164 Alpha processor, available now for samples
and in quantity in a few months. We will be releasing the 433 Mhz motherboard
soon, but I still have no firm date.
I should know more in 2 weeks as when new complete motherboards will be
available at 433 and 500 Mhz. The next version should be ATX form factor,
thus will clean fit in any ATX enclosure without the need of a special
3.3V power supply as the ATX standard has 3.3 volts.
(see: http://www.x86.org/intel.doc/IntelDocs.html for ATX ond other specs.)
It is about time these clone manufacturers standardize on something.
Already a bunch of Intel clones are available in ATX format.
Linux, as far as I know uses the ARC console to run the program that allows
it to boot.  If the ARC sees the drives (Display system configuration menu)
it should be able to boot from it.  We unfortunately do not support, but 
encourage the use of Linux.  Our European division is quite big on Linux.
